<title>USA: N.Sea Brent ends mixed in late U.S. paper trading.</title>
<headline>N.Sea Brent ends mixed in late U.S. paper trading.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>North Sea Brent ended mixed in late U.S. paper trading on Tuesday, traders said.</p>
<p>Two partial April Brents changed hands 100 times apiece at $19.20 and $19.29 a barrel, compared to $19.24 at the IPE settlement in London</p>
<p>A full boat of May Brent moved at $19.15 a barrel, up five cents from the London close.</p>
<p>May/June Brent traded at five cents, consistent with late afternoon talk.</p>
<p>--Patricia Garip-Bertuol NY Energy Desk ((+1 212 859 1620))</p>
</text>
